WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.302
-We're a week into
the Biden administration,

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.370
and Republicans
have made it clear

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.705
they will do everything possible

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.007
to sabotage
the Democrats' agenda,

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:11.143
while moving quickly to quash
the upcoming impeachment trial

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.545
of former
President Donald Trump.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.281
For more on this,
it's time for a Closer Look.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.718
♪♪

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.919
The modern Republican Party

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.455
has no discernible
policies or principles

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.324
other than feigned persecution
and cultural grievances.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.694
Seriously, what is
even one policy

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.295
they've advanced to help
working people?

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.497
"Well, we gave your CEO
a tax cut,

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:34.901
so maybe he'll look more relaxed
in the preflight video."

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:39.305
There are very real,
unprecedented existential crises

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.973
swirling around us
on a daily basis,

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.976
creating suffering and misery
for millions of Americans.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.811
And instead,
the right is obsessed

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:47.614
with trivial garbage like this.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.948 line:0%
-Right around the election,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:52.051 line:0%
I had one million followers
on Twitter.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.253 line:0%
Now I have under 900,000.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.622 line:0%
Really, I mean, literally
in a couple of weeks.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.058 line:0%
I don't know
what's going on there.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.459
-Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:05.265
I was just lighting a prayer
candle for Maria Bartiromo.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.367
That was a truly
harrowing story, Maria.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.335
When people talk about
what we've lost this past year,

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.870
I think first on that list

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.205
is going to be
your Twitter followers.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.040
Thank you for speaking out
about this.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.141
You're like a modern-day

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.042
Erin Brockovich
or Sully Sullenberger.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:19.812
I hope you get your own biopic.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.714
Thousands of people
have been dying a day

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.048
in overwhelmed hospitals.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:25.584
Millions are out of work,
losing their health insurance

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.887
and falling into poverty,
and child hunger is on the rise.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.955
Republicans
and people like Bartiromo

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:32.057
have powerful platforms
with millions of viewers.

00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:34.426
They could spend
any amount of time they want

00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:36.162
talking about any of that.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.364
Instead, they manufacture
dumb grievances

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.732
to distract from real problems

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.667
and make themselves
feel like victims.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.003
It's their entire
business model.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.671
And after Joe Biden got elected,

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.774
they amped it up
to an absurd degree.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.541 line:0%
-Curt Schilling wrote
a social media post

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:53.045 line:0%
defending Donald Trump,
and in 2021, that's not allowed.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.615 line:0%
You could lose
your insurance for that.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.983 line:0%
You could also lose
your bank account, your website,

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.818 line:0%
your access to email
and social media,

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:01.587 line:0%
your ability to communicate
with the outside world,

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:02.755 line:0%
and there's nothing
you can do about it,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.124 line:0%
because you can also
lose your lawyer.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.427 line:0%
No legal representation for you.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.230 line:0%
How long before they cut off
your water and electricity?

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.766 line:0%
Before UPS
won't deliver your packages?

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.367 line:0%
And not to wreck your day,
but guess what?

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:19.038 line:0%
Amazon is now one of America's
biggest grocery providers.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.440 line:0%
Good thing you don't
need to eat.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.542 line:0%
Once politicians attempt
to control what you believe,

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.277 line:0%
they are no longer politicians.

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:27.980 line:0%
They are, by definition,
dictators.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.617 line:0%
And if they succeed in
controlling what you believe,

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.018 line:0%
you are no longer a citizen.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.486 line:0%
You are not a free man.
You are a slave.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:35.822
-If they control
what you believe

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.523
you're no longer a citizen.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.959
If they tell you what to think,
you're no longer free.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.027
And when they tell you
you have to wear

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:44.330
not just a shirt and shoes,
but pants

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.700
to California Pizza Kitchen,
you're a slave.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.903
And how long before they cut off
your water, your electricity?

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:53.106
How long before
they tow your car

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.508
for parking on the sidewalk
outside Chuck E. Cheese?

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.476
Not because you were drunk,
mind you,

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.246
but because you were in a hurry
and you were drunk.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.615
And when you hide
from the police in the ball pit,

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.350
don't be surprised
when they find you,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.819
because those ball pits are
shallower than they look,

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.987
and as an adult man,

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.956
part of you will be
sticking out and visible.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.024
How long before that happens?

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.559
I'll tell you how long.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.763
It happened to me yesterday.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.264
And then this week,
there was yet another,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.301
even more ridiculous example
of this feigned victimhood

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:26.005
when the MyPillow guy famous
for inventing a worse version

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.409
of a thing we've had
for 500 years...

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.777
[ As Mike Lindell ]
"Honey, I've got an idea.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.447
What about, like, a soft thing
for your head at night?"

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.681
"You mean a pillow, honey?"

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:39.886
"Yeah. I'm heading to the lab."

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.055
"Don't rush back."

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.790
Famous for inventing a pillow,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.027
and for spreading
the deranged conspiracy theory

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.164
that China used voting machines
to hack the election,

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.031
went on Fox News to complain

00:03:53.031 --> 00:03:55.367
about his products
getting dropped from stores.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.236 line:0%
-For the crime of having
different opinions.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.439 line:0%
Mike Lindell has just been
banned from Twitter.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.074 line:0%
Several retailers have also
stopped selling his products.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.208 line:0%
That happened today.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.344 line:0%
That would include
Bed, Bath and Beyond,

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.112 line:0%
Kohl's and Kroger.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.080 line:0%
That list is bigger.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.149 line:0%
There's also HEB,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.919 line:0%
the Shopping Channel, ShopHQ.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:17.823 line:0%
I mean, they just keep
turning in their POs

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.426 line:0%
and saying, "We don't want
MyPillow anymore."

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.095
-Dear God, Kroger
and the Shopping Channel

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.497
stopped selling MyPillow?

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.166
Whither freedom?

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:31.270
If George Washington heard this,
he would roll over in his grave,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.041
which is still more comfortable
than rolling on to MyPillow.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.309
People don't know this,

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:39.311
but that's actually what
caused the Revolution.

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.246
The British told Thomas Paine

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:43.215
he couldn't sell his line
of toilet seat cushions

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:44.683
in the town square anymore

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.786
because his opinions
were too controversial,

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:51.824
so Thomas Paine started
the Revolutionary War.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.593
Thomas Paine's
toilet seat cushions.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.329
Time to drain the main vein?
Do it on a Paine?

00:04:56.329 --> 00:05:01.967
Paine's toilet seat cushions.
It's just common sense.

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.203
That was a joke for
my 8th-grade history teacher.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.505
Shout out to, um...

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.741
I cannot remember.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.176
Well, I guess that's why
he or she always told me

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:13.179
I was so bad at history.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.880
I just see a blur.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.449
They were definitely
by a chalkboard.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:20.886
Also, I should say,
I'm skeptical of big tech, too.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:21.954
So we're lots of progressives.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.055
Don't get me wrong,

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.924
I love having Donald Trump
off Twitter,

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.259
not to mention
all the other toxic racists

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.595
and conspiracy theories
that have been booted off.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.398
But my concern is that
these companies are monopolies,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.467
which is why I think
we should follow the lead

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.868
of Elizabeth Warren
and Bernie Sanders

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.236
and break them up.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.971
Just because you agree
with Jack Dorsey on some things

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.140
doesn't mean you will agree
on the next thing.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.910
And if you don't believe me,
may I present Exhibit Beard?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.246
But as for stores not wanting
to carry your product,

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.014
you lied and said
the election was rigged

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:50.916
and tried to get the president
to overturn it.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:53.085
You can't be the public face
of your company

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.988
and the public face of an
attempt to overthrow democracy

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.723
and not expect there
to be some fallout.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:58.724
You could have named your
company

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.859
"SleepWell" or
"Gravel in a Sack"

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:04.663
and stayed in the shadows,
but no, had to be "MyPillow."

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:07.066
And you had to call yourself
"the MyPillow guy"

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.869
and be in all the commercials
like some knock-off Tom Selleck.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.203
Well, listen up.

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:13.573
It takes more than a mustache
to be a spokesman, buddy.

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:14.974
You need that Selleck charm.

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:16.909
By the way, I got one of those

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.978
reverse mortgages
he told me about.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:22.881
And in the end,
he did take my house,

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:25.852
But he was an absolute gentleman
about it.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:27.520
A true blue one!

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:31.357
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:33.125
This is all they have --

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.427
whining and obstruction,
imagined grievances,

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:37.029
paranoia
and conspiracy theories.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.931
Even Donald Trump,
the former president

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.399
who spent two months
deeply engaged

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.668
in a concerted effort
to overthrow democracy

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.870
and install himself
as an unelected dictator

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.106
who incited a violent
insurrection of seditionists,

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.508
who ransacked the Capitol,

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:52.078
is in their minds, a victim.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:54.747
-I don't even think there's
a basis for impeachment.

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:57.583
Now they're going to turn around
and bring about impeachment.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.718
Yet they say they're for unity.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:03.088
I mean, they beat him up
before he got into office.

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:05.791
They're beating him up
after he leaves office.

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:09.662
I mean, at some point,
I mean, give the man a break.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.831
-At some point?
It's been three weeks.

00:07:12.831 --> 00:07:14.166
Give the man a break?

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:15.902
At some point later
in the same month?

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.936
But, yes, please,
for once in his life,

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:19.404
give poor Donald Trump a break.

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:22.274
This poor man, who,
despite having bone spurs,

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:25.344
pulled himself up
by his bootstraps.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.578
You know how much
bone spurs hurt

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:29.849
when you're pulling on boots
with straps?

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:31.216
This man worked his way up,

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:34.319
worked his way up
from hardscrabble roots,

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.887
using just his hands,

00:07:35.887 --> 00:07:37.956
cashed a million dollar
check from his father,

00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:40.092
toiled long days
in a dark casino

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.961
and long nights inhaling
wind song and glitter

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:43.295
at Studio 54.

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:45.131
He made it in business
the hard way

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.599
by bravely cheating on his taxes

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:48.000
and refusing to pay
his contractors.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.436
And worst of all, he has
to drive his own golf cart.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.739
I mean, look at that poor man,
so exhausted he's about

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.140
to fall over.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.676
Seriously,
all Trump, his entire life,

00:07:57.676 --> 00:07:59.479
all he's had are breaks.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.046
He's famously
the dumbest man alive.

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:03.182
He has no discernible talents
or skills.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.318
If Trump weren't born rich,
he'd be the old guy

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.585
working at the bowling alley

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:08.387
who gets busted
for huffing shoe spray.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:12.124
[ Imitates spraying ]
"This here kills COVID."

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.693
[ Imitates spraying ]
"I just got an idea.

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:15.060
What if we put
something comfortable

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.228
on top of the box spring?"

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:18.598
"A mattress?"
"Yeah, the MyMattress."

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:22.067
Hello, patent office?
It's me again.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.869
No, I'm not calling
about pencils this time.

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:26.639
It's a new idea."

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.206
Also, the last point
I'll make, Nikki Haley,

00:08:28.206 --> 00:08:30.242
maybe instead of
asking Democrats

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:31.610
to give Trump a break,

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:35.514
you should ask yourselves
why you, the Republican Party,

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.550
gave him so many.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.485
For four years,
you excuse his behavior.

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:41.153
So, of course, he kept
pushing it.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.855
You're like a rich parent,
asking the court for mercy

00:08:43.855 --> 00:08:45.324
for their bratty teen,
saying,

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.725
"Please, Your Honor,
give him a break.

00:08:46.725 --> 00:08:48.026
It's what I always did.

00:08:48.026 --> 00:08:49.929
Every time he stole or lied
or cheated on a test,

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:52.264
I looked him in the eye and
said, 'You're my special boy,

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:54.333
and nothing you do will ever
change how much I love you.'

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.768
And yet he kept stealing
and lying and cheating.

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:58.203
And I kept forgiving him,
sometimes even helped him.

00:08:58.203 --> 00:08:59.671
I believe the legal term
is aiding and abetting.

00:08:59.671 --> 00:09:00.940
And now he's accused

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.674
of hijacking a bus
full of senior citizens

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:04.376
and taking their pills
and then forcing the seniors

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:06.111
to rout liquor stores for them
to get their pills back,

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:07.579
something I know
for a fact he did,

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:09.047
because it's long
been his dream.

00:09:09.047 --> 00:09:11.517
Well, all I can say to you,
Your Honor, is give him a break.

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:13.552
It's got to work
one of these days."

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.688
It's hard at this point
to reach any conclusion

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:17.156
other than
that the Republican Party

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:20.358
is fine with what Trump did
and they'd be fine with it

00:09:20.358 --> 00:09:23.629
if he did it again or even
if he did something worse.

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:26.065
It's a party that is radicalized
against democracy

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:27.533
in favor of authoritarianism.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:30.702
There is nothing, nothing Trump
could do to antagonize them,

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:33.105
not because they're cowards,
although they are,

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:34.606
but because
they agree with them.

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:37.410
At a certain point, we just have
to take them at their word.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.811
If you sit down to dinner
with some friends

00:09:39.811 --> 00:09:41.981
and one of them says, "You know
what's delicious?

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.650
Human flesh,"
you might think it's a joke.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.984
But when you go
to their apartment

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:47.586
and they're sautéing
a human hand,

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:51.256
you have to ask yourself,
"Is Gary a cannibal?"

00:09:51.256 --> 00:09:54.526
And then, by the way,
if you stay for dinner,

00:09:54.526 --> 00:09:56.596
you're a cannibal, too,

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:59.332
even if you have salad
the next day.

00:09:59.332 --> 00:10:00.967
45 Senate Republicans
voted Tuesday

00:10:00.967 --> 00:10:03.102
to dismiss
Trump's impeachment trial.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:05.404
At some point,
you just have to accept

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:07.139
that the reason they don't want
to convict Trump

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:09.942
for inciting an insurrection
to overthrow a democracy

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:12.611
is they don't care
that he incited an insurrection

00:10:12.611 --> 00:10:13.879
to overthrow democracy

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.347
and they wouldn't care
if he tried it again.

00:10:15.347 --> 00:10:18.550
Instead, they're once again
framing Trump as the victim

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.453
and casting the Democrats calls
for accountability

00:10:21.453 --> 00:10:23.322
as a demand for vengeance.

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:27.660
-This impeachment is nothing
more than a partisan exercise

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.462
designed to further divide
the country.

00:10:30.462 --> 00:10:34.600
Democrats claim to want
to unify the country,

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.802
but impeaching
a former president,

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:41.039
a private citizen,
is the antithesis of unity.

00:10:41.039 --> 00:10:42.340
-It's vindictive.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.477
This is all about
the left's demands for revenge.

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:49.114
-They hate Donald J. Trump,
and they're engaging in an act

00:10:49.114 --> 00:10:50.449
that I think is petty.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.017
I think it is retribution.

00:10:52.017 --> 00:10:53.418
I think it is vindictive.

00:10:53.418 --> 00:10:54.886
And I think it's
a waste of time.

00:10:54.886 --> 00:10:59.191
And so, to coin a phrase,
I think it's time to move on.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:00.993
-Man, Ted Cruz,
you really have no shame.

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:03.295
Also, first of all, shave, dude.

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:05.364
You look like the Unabomber
at a custody hearing.

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:07.999
Second, of course,
you want to move on.

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:09.502
You did this even after the mob

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.336
stormed the Capitol
to overturn the election.

00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:13.572
You still voted
to overturn the election.

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:15.441
You're like a guy
who robs a bank,

00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.342
and then even after it
all goes south,

00:11:17.342 --> 00:11:20.179
you still get caught and use
the money to buy a Porsche.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:22.948
"I want to feel the wind
and my scraggly beard."

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:25.818
Also, please stop with this
preposterous talking point

00:11:25.818 --> 00:11:27.586
that impeachment
is somehow divisive.

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:30.322
You know, it's much more
divisive than impeachment?

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:32.724
Trying to throw out the votes
of 81 million Americans,

00:11:32.724 --> 00:11:35.627
then inciting a mob
to violently storm the Capitol

00:11:35.627 --> 00:11:37.129
the overthrow democracy.

00:11:37.129 --> 00:11:40.299
Would you say that's more or
less unifying than impeachment?

00:11:40.299 --> 00:11:44.170
Just be honest and say
you're fine with what Trump did

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.538
and you'd be fine with him
doing it again.

00:11:46.538 --> 00:11:48.607
It would be heinous and evil,
but it would at least

00:11:48.607 --> 00:11:50.075
make this whole debate
much easier.

00:11:50.075 --> 00:11:52.510
Then we wouldn't have to listen
to your [bleep] excuses anymore.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:55.848
I mean, you know what you are.
We know what you are.

00:11:55.848 --> 00:11:58.684
Who are we pretending for?
The kids?

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:01.587
One of our two main political
parties is fully radicalized

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:03.689
against democracy
in favor of authoritarianism.

00:12:03.689 --> 00:12:05.591
It's a movement
of powerful interests

00:12:05.591 --> 00:12:07.225
backed by wealthy
corporate patrons,

00:12:07.225 --> 00:12:09.828
fueled by imagined grievances
and conspiracy theories.

00:12:09.828 --> 00:12:12.364
We can't ignore it.
We can't look away from it.

00:12:12.364 --> 00:12:14.300
We can't just shrug
our shoulders and say...

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.301
-I don't know
what's going on there.

00:12:16.301 --> 00:12:17.836
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:17.836 --> 00:12:21.673
♪♪

00:12:21.673 --> 00:12:23.609
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:24.877
